From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Narfinger <Narfinger@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 11:38:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] backport: deny: Rustsec for rusqlite advisory (#49746)

This adds an exception to rustsec advisory for rusqlite. Currently the
rusqlite version cannot be updated as sea-query-rusqlite is dependent on
0.38. With >=0.39 being safe. This is a vulnerability in libsqlite which
is bundled in.

https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0459

Testing: No tests for deny.toml.

Signed-off-by: Narfinger <Narfinger@users.noreply.github.com>

Fork note: upstream b8e2c9652a1, which came after Servo 0.8.0, backported
unchanged. On 0.8.0 the cargo-deny step of `./mach test-tidy` fails on
this advisory. Drop this patch at the first sync onto a release that
contains #49746, where it applies empty.

Validation: `./mach test-tidy` on ohos-main 8ca6843c7f9 with this commit: the cargo-deny step no longer reports the libsqlite3-sys advisory (RUSTSEC-2026-0459); the libz-sys and chrono advisories, which the next two backports handle, remain.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; backported unchanged by the agent)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
---
 deny.toml | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/deny.toml b/deny.toml
index 210b14b8b7e..7e295b5fa46 100644
--- a/deny.toml
+++ b/deny.toml
@@ -49,6 +49,10 @@ ignore = [
     # The crate `zvariant_derive` is unmaintained. Wait for `atspi-common` to start
     # using `zbus`.
     "RUSTSEC-2026-0372",
+
+    # rusqlite can not be independently updated as sea-query-rusqlite needs update.
+    "RUSTSEC-2026-0459",
+
 ]
 
 # This section is considered when running `cargo deny check licenses`
